WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.703
-Who are you?
-I lead a group of immortals.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:04.937
An army, I guess.

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:07.273
Soldiers, fighters, like you.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.941
Look...

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.845
you've got questions, kid.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.247
I get it.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.015
You want answers?

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:19.151
Get back in the car.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:20.953
-That was a clip from
"The Old Guard,"

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.888
which is available
to stream now on Netflix.

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:25.925
Here's more of my conversation
with Charlize Theron.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:29.194
Another really cool thing
about this film is --

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.031
obviously,
your co-star is a woman,

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.967
directed by a black woman.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.802
And I believe the producers --

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:40.539
Three of the producers
were women, yourself included.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:41.908
How was that experience?

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:45.144
Was it -- Did you feel the
difference being out there?

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:50.417
-Yeah. I mean, listen,

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.519
there's a sadness attached to
the fact that it feels so great,

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:57.790
because it does feel very
unusual, and that's not right.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.961
We shouldn't have --
You know, when I look back on my

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:06.032
over-25-year career,
it's really sad how often --

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:10.069
how little I've experienced
with more women than men.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.305
And so, you know,
it was really nice on this

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:17.176
to come on set and be
surrounded by women.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:19.345
There was just a
different energy about it.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.680
And, you know, just not women,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.615
but, like,
really talented women.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.718
Like, that is the other thing
that's always so crazy to me.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:29.088
Like, it's not that hard to find
really talented women

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.356
in all departments --
not just in front of the camera,

00:01:31.356 --> 00:01:32.925
but behind the camera.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.262
And so, I --
You know, I think --

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.231
I really do think we have
to just --

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.266
We have to keep
the pressure on our industry

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.836
to kind of sustain
this kind of storytelling,

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:48.574
because it is really --
I almost swore -- F'ing awesome.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:49.642
It really is.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.811
-[ Laughs ] That's alright.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.046
We would have happily beeped
that out for you.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:56.416
That's the least we could do.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.784
And this isn't
giving anything away,

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.152
but it is -- You know, again,

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.623
it's based on this comic
that tells a longer story.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.892
It certainly seems set up
to tell more story.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.961
And so that must be exciting
too, that, you know,

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.731
you have this very
female-forward action film

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:15.334
that is lined up to make more.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.503
-Yeah. With another
female character,

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:18.938
which I'm really excited about.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.174
The character of Quynh
is kind of teased in this.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:24.744
She's Andy's
kind of right-hand person.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.347
She's was --
The two of them were the first,

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.148
and there's obviously
a relationship there

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.618
that we didn't really explore
in this film.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:35.087
So I'm excited, if we get the
chance to make another one,

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:37.756
to explore that, because then
we're just, you know,

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:40.793
adding another
female into the mix,

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.696
which I think will make it
really interesting.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.465
-I do feel like
I'd like to finish --

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.735
The last time you were on the
show, we talked about

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:53.505
I think both of our favorite
female superhero, Rihanna.

00:02:53.505 --> 00:02:57.776
And you and Rihanna
shared a publicist.

00:02:57.776 --> 00:03:00.313
You told a really funny story
about her burning you

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:03.983
with a T-shirt of an e-mail
where the publicist

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:08.321
basically called her -- called
Rihanna her favorite client,

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.523
and then she sent that on
a T-shirt to you.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.926
I then had the good fortune of
going day drinking with Rihanna.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:17.063
And, yeah,
it's really good times

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.598
to have any connection to her
in the real world.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.535
-She is -- she is everything.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:26.372
I had the luxury of doing some
night drinking with her.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.175
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah, out in London.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.811
And it was some of
the best night drinking

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.980
I've ever done
in my entire life.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.916
-Yeah, I should note
that we day-drank,

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.352
and then I went home to fall
asleep in my foyer.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.654
And I got the sense
that that wasn't

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.155
the last drinking she did.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:46.759
I got the sense that, like, the
most drinking I had done

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.596
in like years was just, like,
warm-up stretches for her.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:53.699
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.334
So, I'm very jealous.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.904
I'm very jealous that you
got the other half of it.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.639
-She needs to be in
the next "Old Guard."

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.807
"Ri-Ri."
-Yeah.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.742
There you go. There you go.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.844
See? We put together
some casting, as well.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.546
Charlize, I really do hope
the next time I see you,

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:08.615
it's in person.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.550
Congrats on the film.
It's so much fun.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.784
And I hope to see you soon.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.086
-Thank you so much, Seth.
Nice to see you.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:15.420
-Nice to see you, too.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.690
-Next time, we can talk about
all the "Moby-Dick" stuff

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.025
in the background there.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:22.394
-This is what I --
I'm at my in-laws's house,

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:23.495
so I can't choose decor.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:25.698
-[ Laughing ] Oh, I'm sorry.
Okay.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.567
-That's all right.
[ Both laugh ]

